 "voice": [
  {
   "t": 0.3,
   "text": "Thirty-nine thousand dollars, in an exporter's wallet, the day the goods ship. This is Hisab on Monad."
  },
  {
   "t": 6.853,
   "text": "Small exporters wait ninety days to get paid. Here, a lender pool advances the cash instead. This is the live console on Monad testnet, with three roles and three wallets."
  },
  {
   "t": 18.219,
   "text": "Wallets are burners by default. Or connect a browser wallet, or log in with email through Privy."
  },
  {
   "t": 24.212,
   "text": "Exporter first. One click funds gas, registers a forty-eight thousand seven hundred fifty dollar shipping bill, and seeds two on-time invoices of history."
  },
  {
   "t": 33.839,
   "text": "That history earns tier one: eighty percent advance, at twelve and a half percent. So the offer is thirty-nine thousand A U S D."
  },
  {
   "t": 43.998,
   "text": "Now a lender. Mint some test A U S D, deposit a hundred thousand, and the pool mints shares against it."
  },
  {
   "t": 51.128,
   "text": "Next, the buyer. They sign an E I P seven-twelve message. No signature, no financing."
  },
  {
   "t": 58.937,
   "text": "Back to the exporter, who accepts the offer. The receivable locks to the pool, and thirty-nine thousand lands in the same transaction. Confirmed in about three seconds, end to end."
  },
  {
   "t": 70.709,
   "text": "Try to finance the same bill twice, and the contract refuses. Double financing, blocked."
  },
  {
   "t": 78.562,
   "text": "Now the buyer pays. One transaction, three legs. Forty thousand to the pool, principal plus interest. A twenty-six dollar fee. And eight thousand seven hundred twenty-two to the exporter."
  },
  {
   "t": 91.091,
   "text": "Paid on time, so the exporter climbs to tier two: eighty-eight percent advance, at eleven and a half. Register the next invoice, and the offer jumps to forty-two thousand nine hundred."
  },
  {
   "t": 103.796,
   "text": "And the lender? The share price ticked up. That is interest, earned from a real shipment."
  },
  {
   "t": 110.7,
   "text": "Open the explorer. Every state links to its Monad transaction: registered, acknowledged, financed, paid."
  },
  {
   "t": 117.718,
   "text": "Short pays are marked partial. A missed due date drops the exporter to tier zero. Twenty-eight contract tests pass, and the legacy SWIFT path is still there."
  },
  {
   "t": 127.298,
   "text": "Why Monad? Fast finality. Every step you just saw confirmed in about three seconds. And A U S D is the single asset, a mock on testnet."
  },
  {
   "t": 136.764,
   "text": "Hisab on Monad. Live now, code on GitHub. Built with Monad, A U S D, and Privy."
  }
 ],
